1:Mahjong Soul Shrine
2:player
3:Good afternoon, everyone! Today is such a beautiful day, right?
4:Greeting everyone energetically with a wide and open smile, I radiate a sunny, cheerful, and positive aura as I walk into the mahjong room of the Mahjong Soul Shrine where I plan to have a fulfilling day petting cats and dogs, playing mahjong, and meeting many fantastic Jyanshi after sleeping in till now.
5:However, an unusual aura fills the air after I find a table that seems to have good feng shui and sit down after greeting the three Jyanshi there. They tacitly stop what they are doing.
6:Jyanshi A
7:I suddenly remember that I have some homework to finish. Sorry, I'll be leaving now.
8:Jyanshi B
9:Wait for me! We can do it together. Sorry, I'll be leaving now too.
10:Jyanshi C
11:Er... I also need to leave.
12:Hey! You... You three... Wait up... Don't run away so quickly! Why are you even pretending to be young junior high school students when your hairline has receded so much already, you jerks!!!
13:The three Jyanshi disappear without looking back.
14:I glance helplessly at the now-empty seats and turn to look at the other tables that have empty seats. After meeting my gaze, the Jyanshi who are looking at me curiously all lower their heads and stare at the backside of their tiles like they are deep in thought, just like students who are afraid their class teacher will make them answer questions.
15:Ichihime
16:Master, this is terrible, nyaa. Nobody wants to play with you, nyaa. Wanjirou, think of something, nyaa!
17:Wanjirou
18:Why don't you try writing the words "Chiori Mikami is definitely not following me today" on your forehead and see if anyone will play with you, woof.
19:Master, shall we give that a try, nyaa?
20:It's okay... Instead of trying that nonsense... Why don't you two stay here and play with me...?
21:...Hey! Where's the dog?! Where's the cat?!
22:The dog and cat strategist duo has instantly disbanded on the spot.
23:I sigh and find myself unable to blame them. After all, today's situation is caused by a certain young lady who follows me around like my shadow.
24:Ever since my relationship with Chiori Mikami became friendlier, she has started to see me as an interesting toy instead of a commoner. Although she hasn't said this explicitly, this is what her actions have been telling me!!!
25:I know because I have noticed that she is a player in any game I play, whether it is a board game, mahjong, or even an ordinary game of cards. What's more, her goal seems to have changed from simply winning the game to defeating all her opponents, especially {var:player_nickname}.
26:Over time, people started spreading a rumor that as long as I am playing a game, a blond girl will appear and dominate everyone who is playing, which has made it difficult to find strangers who are willing to play with me during this time.
27:I look at the three empty seats again. Oh well, I might as well ask everyone in the group chat if they can play mahjong right now while I wait for Chiori Mikami to arrive. The only thing I have lots of in One Han City is friends.

29:Miki Nikaidou
30:...
31:Nana Shiraishi
32:Any luck?
33:I put down my phone and shake my head, looking apologetically at the two people who are sitting to my left and my right before looking at the empty seat opposite me.
34:Who would have thought that I would find two players to play with so soon and that Chiori Mikami still hasn't appeared today?
35:She and Riu are both not picking up. They'd have already arrived by this time in the past. This is strange...
36:What a surprise! You two have always been inseparable, but are not together today. Haha.
37:Well... to be honest, I'm quite surprised too.
38:Junior, did you do anything to offend Chiori without realizing it?
39:I... don't think so.
40:But when I think of the "shadowless kick attacks" that Chiori Mikami has been making for no apparent reason recently, I feel like I can't completely rule out that possibility.
41:Haha, you're obviously worried, {var:player_nickname}. Why don't you go and see how she is doing?
42:Huh? But I'm the one who invited you here to play mahjong...
43:Yeah, so hurry up and comfort the girl before thinking of how to make it up to me. I won't forgive you easily if you aren't sincere enough.
44:Haha, I'll be fine. You can just treat me and my classmates to afternoon tea next time! Don't worry, I'll pick a day when more people are helping out at the club for you to make good on this promise!
45:Haha, sigh. Okay, sorry about this. I'll meet up with you another day!
47:Around Chiori Mikami's House
48:Chiori Mikami's house is in a beautiful villa complex in One Han City. Although this isn't my first time here, I'm still shocked by the luxuriousness of this place. For example, the movement-tracking electronic cameras around her house seem to be installed as part of a security system upgrade due to the previous uninvited guest incident.
49:It doesn't look like anything has happened. Did I really make her angry by accident?
50:*Ding-dong* I press the electronic doorbell at the entrance of Chiori Mikami's house and wait silently.
51:Soon after, the camera of the electronic doorbell emits a green flash when someone checks who has come knocking. The strange thing is that the person answers the door silently without making a sound.
52:I wave at the camera in confusion.
53:Chiori? Riu?
54:*Click*
55:The only response I get is the sound of the call being cut off.
56:???
57:Um... Could something really have happened?
58:A wealthy young lady living alone in a large villa in the city, whose parents are not home during most of the year, and a young maid who takes care of her daily life. If this combination were to appear in Getham City next door, they would have been coveted by various criminal gangs already. Suddenly my mind is filled with all kinds of crimes that could have happened, and I'm even ready to call the police.
59:Suddenly, the door opens with a click.
60:Chiori Mikami
61:Good afternoon, {var:player_nickname}. Why have you come to see me today?
62:The door is open, and Chiori Mikami looks very lively, but... her sunny and cheerful appearance at the door reminds me of the deliberate act I put up when I was trying to convince the mahjong players to stay this noon. It looks... extremely unnatural!
63:Chiori, are you okay?
64:Huh? I'm in my own home. What could possibly go wrong? Haha! You say such funny things, {var:player_nickname}.
65:If you're here to ask me to play with you, {var:player_nickname}, then I'm sorry to say that I'm busy right now. Maybe we can play together another time?
66:But you're so polite that it looks like something is wrong.
67:...Why are you still here?
68:Chiori Mikami looks a little anxious. She moves closer to me and lowers her voice, making the expression she usually makes when she bullies me. She even waves her fist at me like Riu Kujou does.
69:Ah, this is more like it! Feeling relieved, I think that it seems like she really might be busy with something she can't tell me about.
70:Okay, I feel better now that I know you're fine. See you later.
71:Yeah, see you later, {var:player_nickname}. Take care.
72:As I prepare to leave, I hear the unfamiliar voice of a middle-aged woman from inside the house.
73:Chiori, has a friend come to visit you?
74:Stunned, I stop and turn around. My eyes are drawn above Chiori Mikami's head towards a neatly dressed woman who has just walked up to the door.
75:She has the same dazzling golden hair as Chiori Mikami, but it's shoulder-length and tucked behind her ears, giving her a calm and intellectual appearance.
76:Hi, it's nice to meet you. I'm Chiori Mikami's mother.
77:...Oh, hello!
78:Chiori Mikami's House
79:Chiori Mikami stands in front of me, holding a fine tray with exquisite snacks and hot coffee on it. She then starts to transfer them onto the coffee table in front of me.
80:Here you are. The sugar and milk are on the side, so please add them if you want.
81:Um... Thanks, Chiori.
82:You. Are. Welcome.
83:If I can ignore the murderous look in her eyes, her stiff smile and sweet voice make me really want to take out my phone and record the scene of Chiori Mikami serving me politely... That is, if I can also ignore Mrs. Mikami sitting next to me.
84:Sitting prudishly on the sofa, I quickly go over everything Chiori Mikami has told me about her mother in my head. She is an internationally renowned surgeon, a professional at the top of her profession who travels around the world all year round and is just as busy as her husband, who is a physics professor. As a result, they can only hire a maid to take care of their daughter. She is a very capable career-oriented woman.
85:I didn't expect her to be at home today. That would explain why Chiori Mikami didn't follow me to play mahjong today.
86:Mrs. Mikami
87:It looks like you're Chiori's close friend. What's your name?
88:Hearing her question, I quickly sit up straight, then I introduce myself to her briefly and explain the reason for my visit.
89:I see. Thank you for caring so much about Chiori's safety. She hasn't really been on her phone today, and I think Riu didn't pick up either because she is taking an exam today. I heard that it's a make-up exam for a special training class, so I haven't seen her either.
90:Oh, I see... I understand then.
91:Thanks again for caring so much that you came all the way here to check up on her.
92:Don't mention it. That's what friends do. However, my unexpected visit seems to have interrupted your time together with Chiori.
93:Haha, that's fine. I'm delighted to have the opportunity to meet one of Chiori's friends. In fact, I'm quite surprised. The last time I was here, Chiori stayed at home with Riu for the entire day... Chiori, why didn't you tell me you made such a close friend?
94:...T-There's nothing special about it. It's not like we're thaaaat close. We're just normal...
95:Hmm?
96:We're just normal friends. We're definitely not close enough to spend every day together!
97:Mrs. Mikami looks back and forth between me and Chiori Mikami thoughtfully with a hint of curiosity. Although her gaze is still kind, I feel like she can see right through me in close detail.
98:Oh...? So what you're saying is that you don't have to, but you do actually spend every day together?
99:Although she isn't wrong, something sounds strange about her words. For a moment, Chiori Mikami and I are unable to say anything to refute her, and we both look at her anxiously.
100:Haha, you don't need to be nervous. I'm really glad that Chiori has made a new friend, but... I rarely get the opportunity to hear about what Chiori does with her friends. If it's okay with you, {var:player_nickname}, can you tell me more about that?
101:Huh?
102:Of course, you can just say what you can. I'm sure that besides the secrets between you, there are stories that you can share with your parents, right?
104:I agree with Mrs. Mikami and think about what to say. At this time, Mrs. Mikami's mobile phone starts ringing.
105:Sorry, I need to take a phone call.
106:Mrs. Mikami stands and walks over to the dining room beside us to answer the call. The room suddenly becomes quiet - so quiet that we can hear what she is saying.
107:Hello... I'm on leave today. Hmm, no, I'm on leave...
108:On the sofa, Chiori Mikami's eyes follow her mother who is speaking on the phone. After hearing their conversation, she sighs in relief, then turns her head and gives me a quiet good-natured warning.
109:You're not allowed to say anything strange to my mother!
110:You're suddenly afraid that I'll tell on you? Isn't it too late?
111:I also heave a sigh of relief for now and whisper a retort back at her.
112:Just as Chiori Mikami opens her mouth and wants to say something, Mrs. Mikami returns and sits down again. She looks at me expectantly and asks me to tell her some interesting things about Chiori Mikami.
113:I look at Chiori Mikami next to her, who is glaring at me with a warning look in her eyes. What should I say?
114:Tell her nice things
115:I can still tell the difference between having one full meal and many full meals.
116:If I'm inconsiderate of Chiori Mikami's feelings and tell Chiori Mikami's mother about embarrassing or bad things that she has done, damaging her mother's image of her, I think I will be in for a rough time in the future.
117:Ahem, there are many memorable stories of our experiences since we met. In short, Chiori is very attentive, very lovely, and very sweet-natured.
118:Chiori Mikami looks obviously relieved upon hearing this.
119:...Whenever I come over to visit, she will always prepare coffee and snacks for me like today.
120:She's also very intelligent and is very good at playing games. She guides me patiently every time we play together. If I'm tired, she'll even ask Riu to give me a relaxing massage that was originally exclusive to her.
121:Oh, she even gave me a massage once when Riu was away... There was also a time when I accidentally got lost while we were feeding cats in the park, and Chiori patiently guided me back here and prepared a delicious dinner for me...
122:As I speak cheerfully, the smile on Chiori Mikami's face, which had started to relax, becomes more and more stiff.
123:Upon hearing me say more and more outrageous things, behind her mother's back, she quietly mouths the words: "This is not over." Suddenly, she frowns and puts her hand against her cheek.
124:Ouch!
125:Mrs. Mikami's attention is drawn immediately by her cry, successfully interrupting my story-telling.
126:What is it? Do your teeth hurt?
127:Chiori Mikami nods in an aggrieved manner.
128:Tell her the truth
129:I'll worry about tomorrow's dangers tomorrow. The most important thing for people is to live in and enjoy the present.
130:I ignore Chiori Mikami's warning look and decide to report everything I've experienced since meeting Chiori Mikami to her mother.
131:Ahem, there are many memorable stories of our experiences since we met. In short, I've been surprised by how cute, intelligent, and beautiful Chiori is.
132:Chiori Mikami looks obviously relieved upon hearing this, but her expression soon changes because of the twist in my words--
133:But as I got to know her better, I learned that... contrary to her beautiful appearance...
134:Just as I am about to get to the point, behind her mother's back, Chiori Mikami quietly mouths the words: "This is not over." Suddenly, she frowns and puts her hand against her cheek.
135:Mrs. Mikami's attention is drawn immediately by her cry, successfully interrupting my complaint.
136:A hint of helplessness appears in Mrs. Mikami's eyes, and she looks down at her watch.
139:Chiori has been prone to tooth decay since she was a child, so she needs to have an oral check-up every year. I managed to come back just in time for her check-up this time, so I want to take this opportunity to go with her to learn more about her dental health from the dentist.
140:I see, in that case...
141:Just as I am about to say that I won't get in their way, Mrs. Mikami's mobile phone suddenly starts ringing.
142:Excuse me.
143:Mrs. Mikami picks up the call, interrupting my second attempt to leave.
144:Hello... Sorry, I already said that I'm on leave. Can you get someone else to go... Director?
145:Mrs. Mikami sounds a little surprised. She pauses for a moment, glances at Chiori Mikami, then hurriedly stands and walks to one side before continuing.
146:...What's happened...? I see...
147:Chiori Mikami's eyes move back and forth between her mother and the pillow in her arms, as if she doesn't want to appear too concerned, but the downward-turning corners of her mouth betray her feelings at this moment.
148:Leave in the afternoon? But I need to take my daughter to...
149:Bits and pieces of the phone conversation drift into our ears. Although we can't hear what the other person is saying, this person's words seem to be gradually convincing Mrs. Mikami to change her mind. Her tone gradually changes from being serious to frustrated. In the end, she sighs.
150:Sigh, I understand. About the plane ticket...
151:It sounds like Mrs. Mikami has been asked to go on a business trip at the last minute. What about the dental appointment then...? Just as I was thinking this, Chiori Mikami suddenly puts down the pillow and walks up to the second floor without saying a word. Her footsteps are heavy and make thudding sounds.
152:Mrs. Mikami obviously sees this too. She covers the microphone of the phone and looks at me apologetically.
153:Can you check up on Chiori for me?
154:Um, okay.
155:I happen to also be worried about Chiori Mikami's current situation, so I agree just like that.
156:As soon as I arrive at the second floor, I see Chiori Mikami walking out of her room with Index in her hands. She pauses for a moment when she sees me coming up.
157:What did you come up here for?
158:You looked very angry just now. Is it because you heard that your mother needs to go on a business trip?
159:Hmph... I'm not a child. I won't get angry because of something I'm already used to.
160:Then why did you suddenly come upstairs and get Index?
161:In Chiori Mikami's arms is a familiar-looking bear-shaped bag. I remember her proudly telling me many times that it was a birthday gift from her mother.
162:You idiot. I'm getting ready to leave. Didn't my mother just say that it's time for my dental appointment?
163:But your mother...
164:Hmph, {var:player_nickname}, you're an idiot, a fool, and a dummy. Do you think I can't go to see the dentist just because my mother is busy?
165:Chiori Mikami hugs Index tightly. Without saying another word, she quickly squeezes past me and starts walking downstairs. I hurriedly follow her down.
166:Downstairs, Mrs. Mikami has just finished the phone call. When she sees Chiori Mikami running downstairs, she calls out to her.
167:Chiori, about your dental appointment...
168:Mom, I'll go by myself.
169:Don't you need to go on a business trip? I can go to the dental appointment by myself.
170:Mrs. Mikami frowns and purses her lips.
171:I just told the hospital to book a later flight. This way, we can still go to the dental appointment together, and I can go directly to the airport from there. We...
172:It really isn't necessary, Mom.
173:Chiori Mikami shakes her head resolutely again. She hugs Index tightly and smiles.
174:You just arrived home in the morning, so you'll be exhausted if you run around like this. You should get some rest. I'll really be okay. I usually go there with Riu, so I'm very familiar with the process. You don't need to worry about me.
175:...But Riu isn't here today. You'll be all alone...
176:Based on what I know about Chiori Mikami, I can tell that her calmness and composure are just a front, but she seems to convince Mrs. Mikami. I want to say something, but hesitate. It looks like Mrs. Mikami really doesn't know her daughter that well.
177:Well, if you're really worried, {var:player_nickname} can come with me. {var:player_nickname}, you'll be happy to come with me, right?
178:Chiori Mikami raises her head, grabs my sleeve, and looks at me. For the first time ever, I see her looking at me with a cry for help in her eyes. Shocked by what I see, I hold her hand and look at Mrs. Mikami.
179:Yeah, I can go with Chiori. Everything will be okay.
180:Mrs. Mikami's eyes linger on our clasped hands for a few seconds, then the look of hesitation disappears as she makes up her mind.
181:Okay, thank you, {var:player_nickname}.
182:After exchanging contact details with Mrs. Mikami, Chiori Mikami and I depart for the dental clinic.
183:We'll come back as soon as we can. Maybe we'll make it back before she leaves.
184:Shut up... I'm tired.
185:Chiori?
186:As soon as Mrs. Mikami can no longer see the taxi, the smile on Chiori Mikami's face disappears immediately. She huddles her head and pretends to sleep, and even refuses to talk to me. The atmosphere in the car feels thick like the air has solidified. All I can do is look at her long eyelashes trembling slightly over her stubbornly closed eyes and sigh quietly in my heart.
187:Chiori Mikami... She is really sad this time.
190:The clinic is very quiet, and the smell of disinfectant fills the air. While sitting in the waiting area, I notice that her eyes are staring at a young mother and her son sitting diagonally opposite us. The boy, who looks about three or four years old, is covering the left side of his face and complaining naively in his mother's arms.
191:Little Boy
192:Mommy, it hurts.
194:There, there. It won't hurt anymore after this.
195:Can we not come here if it doesn't hurt?
196:Of course.
197:Then will you take me to the amusement park if we don't come here?
198:...Hmph.
199:The girl next to me snorts softly with eyes filled with envy. At this moment, I don't think anyone can tell that this is the same Chiori Mikami who is known as the demon king who always shows off her might in mahjong dojos.
200:At this time, she is just a child who has had a one-sided disagreement with her mother.
201:Chiori, are you okay...?
202:This is the third time you've asked me this. I'm starting to get sick of it even if you aren't.
203:Oh, since you're fine, do you want to have a... plum candy?
204:Chiori Mikami rolls her eyes at me, then she covers her ears and ignores me.
205:Sure enough, trying to use candy to lighten the mood with a girl who has a decaying tooth isn't a good idea. Just as I am about to change the subject and start again, an explosion of noise breaks out around us.
206:Young Mother
207:You caused this problem in the first place. Why do we have to keep waiting?
208:I look up at the speaker.
209:The person speaking is the mother who was holding her son just now, and the person she is scolding seems to be the dentist who had just come out of the consulting room. The dentist is wearing a mask, but I can tell how frustrated he is feeling at this moment from his dropping eyebrows.
210:Dentist
211:Yes, but you've come here too many times already. We've performed all the necessary examinations and repairs, but we can't find anything wrong with your son. Maybe another doctor will be able to tell you something we can't. You had best make a new appointment as soon as possible.
212:How can you be so irresponsible?! I have taken leave many times to take my son to see a dentist! You have to fix this for me! You also need to repay me for the loss of my working time!
213:The little boy who seems to be at the center of the dispute clings timidly to his mother's leg. The atmosphere becomes tense.
214:It looks like a dispute between a patient and a dentist. Let's not... Chiori?
215:To my surprise, Chiori Mikami suddenly walks away from me and towards them. She speaks to the dentist and the young mother.
216:Hello, why don't you try another way to deal with this? It might resolve your problem.
217:Oh, it's you, Miss Mikami.
218:It looks like this dentist knows Chiori Mikami. He leans over and whispers in Chiori Mikami's ear, then he calls the young mother to one side and starts discussing something with her in a low voice.
219:While they speak, the little boy sits on the chair, biting his lip and looking uneasily in his mother's direction.

221:Then let's perform the inspection once more according to the procedure.
223:Okay.
224:Seeming to have come to some agreement, the young mother waves for the little boy to enter the clinic for another examination.
225:Out of curiosity, I follow Chiori Mikami inside the room. The dentist looks at us, but doesn't say anything, which only makes me more curious than ever.
226:John, tell me if it hurts, okay?
227:John
228:Okay.
229:The dentist asks the child called John to sit on a chair with his mouth wide open, then he turns on the light on one side and aims it at his mouth before poking his right cheek.
230:There's nothing wrong with the filling we added here last time... Are you sure this is where it's hurting?
231:Huh? Just now... I remember John was holding his left cheek when he said it hurt.
232:To my surprise, John hesitates for a while before nodding.
233:After this, everyone understands what is happening. John is lying.
234:John, mom is already so busy. Why do you have to make a joke like this? How can you do something so childish like pretending to have a toothache?!
235:Um... Um...
236:Seeing that his lie has been exposed, John opens his mouth in manic, and his eyes are suddenly filled with tears.
237:Um... I'm sorry, mom...
238:I just want you to spend more time with me...
239:As long as I have a toothache, you'll spend more time with me...
241:You... Sigh... You silly boy... Why can't you just tell me what you want directly...?
242:In the end, both mother and son calm down and apologize to the doctor together. After that, they come over and thank Chiori Mikami warmly.
243:The storm subsided just like that. After watching the mother and her son leave, I give Chiori Mikami a thumbs-up.
244:Hmph!
245:Chiori Mikami turns her head around proudly. After helping them, her mood is no longer as heavy as it was before.
246:The dentist leaves to clean up the consulting room and replenish disposable supplies and asks us to wait for a while. I take this opportunity to ask Chiori a question I've been holding back from since earlier.
