286:The vibration of my phone brings me back to my senses. I wake up my phone and see that I've received a text message from Mrs. Mikami.
288:(Text Message) Okay, I understand. Thank you for telling me this. It's made me realize that I don't understand my daughter well enough. Chiori has always acted extremely independent in front of me, which really has troubled me for some time.
289:(Text Message) I think it's time for us to have a heart-to-heart talk as mother and daughter. At the same time, I hope that I'll have enough time to invite you to come over again the next time I return home on leave. I want to hear more about her and the stories of you two.
290:It looks like Mrs. Mikami understands what I want to tell her. After putting away my phone, I can feel my mood improving slightly.
291:After that, Chiori Mikami and I spend the entire afternoon in the mahjong dojo.
292:By the time we return to her home, the huge villa is empty again, and everything has returned to normal.
293:Find another way to encourage her to go to the airport.
294:Chiori Mikami is a typical tsundere in One Han City. When she says no, she is often thinking of something else in her heart.
295:A tsundere of her level calls for harsh and drastic measures...
296:Fine, you can play mahjong. I'm familiar with this area. Turn left at the next two corners and you'll find a dojo there. It has a nice environment, and the Jyanshi are quite skilled too. You can go now.
297:Chiori Mikami looks at me warily after I surrender suddenly.
298:What do you mean?
299:Nothing. You can play mahjong. I can go to the airport alone. After all, Mrs. Mikami wants to hear more stories about us. I'm sure she'll be happy to see me if I go there to say goodbye to her.
300:!
301:Oh, just for the record, I invited you, but you don't want to go. If I accidentally say anything to your mother... Hehe... ouch! Don't hit me there!
303:Due to the almost tangible resentment flowing around Chiori Mikami, the taxi driver looks frequently at us curiously in the back.
304:Driver
305:Calm down, little lady. What time is the flight?
306:No, you can drive slowly. The slower the better. In fact, it's best if we never arrive.
307:Haha... little girl, you really know how to make jokes.
308:The driver swallows and then steps hard on the accelerator. I get the feeling that he using his full power as he starts driving wildly.
309:At the same time, with great difficulty due to the bumps and the recoil, I take out my phone and send a text message to Mrs. Mikami.
310:Five minutes later, my phone vibrates gently. I take it out and see that Mrs. Mikami has sent me a reply, and her message makes me feel relieved immediately...
311:I look at Chiori Mikami next to me, who has started to play mahjong online because she is angry and doesn't want to talk to me. Very good, everything is going according to plan.
313:Urgh...
314:The taxi driver leaves proudly, leaving Chiori Mikami and me holding onto some posts at the airport so that we don't fall from the motion sickness-induced dizziness.
315:I was careless. I got motion sickness because I kept sending text messages to Mrs. Mikami, and Chiori Mikami got motion sickness because she was playing mahjong online.
316:Y-You're so useless! I got motion sickness because I was playing mahjong. How did you also end up getting motion sickness?
317:...I...
318:I can't tell her that I've been secretly sending text messages to Mrs. Mikami.
319:That's not the point. Send your mother a message to see where she is now.
320:Huh? You still haven't contacted her? We're already at the airport!
321:Well... Hey, I thought you didn't want to come here to see her. Why are you so concerned about the details?
322:I don't want to see her, but... but we're here anyway... Arghhh! Hurry up! Call her now!
323:Yes, yes, yes.
324:This is great. My flight has been delayed by an hour, and I was just thinking of what to do during this time. It's perfect that you've come.
325:Chiori, did you not tell me you're coming because you wanted to give me a surprise?
326:I-It's because I wasn't sure that we would get here in time. I don't want to put any extra burden on you.
327:There's no such thing. You'll never put any burden on me by coming to see me off. I'm very happy you're here.
328:R-Really...?
329:Unlike how she was at home, Mrs. Mikami seems much more enthusiastic now, which surprises Chiori Mikami. However, it's obvious that she has relaxed because of this.
330:What do you want to eat, Chiori? You can place your order over there. Can you also order some food for {var:player_nickname} and me?
331:Okay, leave it to me.
332:Without wasting any time, Chiori Mikami goes to the counter to order food. From how excited she seems while moving, I can tell that she is in a much better mood after seeing her mother. Upon seeing this, Mrs. Mikami and I turn around and exchange an understanding look.
333:Thanks for sending me that message, {var:player_nickname}.
334:You're welcome. Anyone would do the same.
335:Yes, on our way to the airport in a taxi, I sent Mrs. Mikami a text message to tell her that Chiori Mikami had very keenly noticed that the boy was lying at the clinic a little earlier.
336:Mrs. Mikami has a sharp mind. She replied to my message quickly and took the initiative to ask me more about my observations of Chiori Mikami, then she said she knew what she needed to do and told me she would wait for us at the airport.
337:Mrs. Mikami's gaze becomes gentle when she looks at Index sitting upright on Chiori Mikami's seat.
338:Due to the special nature of our professions, when Chiori was little, Chiori's father and I could only give Chiori gifts like this to make up for the time we couldn't spend with her. Since then, my husband and I have been both proud and surprised by the independence she showed us.
339:We have tried asking her tentatively if she wanted to spend more time with us, but she has always refused and told us to do what we need to do. After that, Riu started accompanying her, and they got along very well. Over time, we really thought that she really was used to living more independently and freely.
340:I never realized that this is just a facade of her strong personality. As a mother, I find it quite shameful that I need an outsider to tell me what my daughter really thinks.
341:I see. Well, you shouldn't blame yourself for this. You know what Chiori's personality is like. If she has decided to hide her true thoughts, no one can convince her otherwise.
342:Thank you for the words of consolation. It seems that just being a mother in the standard sense of the word isn't enough. From now on, I need to become a friend she can trust.
343:Haha, that would be great. Chiori would be overjoyed.
344:However, it's indeed impossible for a mother who doesn't usually communicate a lot with her daughter to quickly change the way she interacts with her daughter.
345:In the restaurant at the airport, the three of us eat burgers and fries in silence.
346:Just now, after Chiori Mikami returned from ordering food, Mrs. Mikami tried to find a topic to chat with her, but she didn't know what to say after a while, and the three of us are now just staring at each other without saying anything. To break the awkward atmosphere, I think about it and make a suggestion.
347:Why don't the three of us play a game of three-player mahjong online to pass the time?
348:Three-player mahjong?
349:You idiot! That's too rude!
350:No way! Mahjong is really interesting! Don't you also enjoy playing it a lot?
351:You idiot! Shut up!
352:...Okay.
353:Mom?
354:I might not know very much about other things like the latest trendiest toy or board games, but mahjong has already been popular since I was a child, and I still remember the rules very clearly. Why don't we play one game then? But how will we play it? There are no mahjong tiles here.
355:Upon hearing her mother's words, Chiori Mikami starts to calm down and glares at me.
356:Mom, I'll help you download a mahjong game. You can play it on your mobile phone after that.
357:Oh, okay.
358:Although she is a little rusty at the very beginning, Mrs. Mikami quickly shows her domineering side after she becomes familiar with the rules again.
359:Kita.
360:At some times, I even get the feeling that I'm playing mahjong against two Chiori Mikamis.
361:Tsumo!
362:In the end, Chiori Mikami wins this game, and Mrs. Mikami puts down her phone feeling like she hasn't had enough yet.
363:Haha, it's very interesting. Chiori plays so much better than I did when I was little.
364:Mom, I play better than many adults!
365:Oh, really? Then I need to practice harder to fight for the honor of all adults.
366:Eh? Mom, you'll continue playing this game?
367:Yeah, this online mahjong game isn't bad at all, and it doesn't take that much time to play one game. I'll get your father to download it too. This way, we'll be able to make some time to play this game together and talk about how we're doing even when we are in different cities. What do you think about that?
368:As Mrs. Mikami speaks, she reaches out and touches Chiori Mikami's face, a bit unpracticed.
369:Mom and dad both want to become your friend. Will you let us?
370:...Okay!
371:Chiori Mikami smiles from the bottom of her heart.
372:Seeing the smile on her face, Mrs. Mikami and I also start smiling.
373:*Ding-dong*-- An airport announcement starts playing, and a gentle and polite female voice issues a reminder that passengers can now start boarding the plane for Mrs. Mikami's flight.
374:The plane carrying Mrs. Mikami takes off from the airport. Chiori Mikami and I look up and watch as the plane flies higher and higher until it disappears above the clouds.
375:I look at Chiori Mikami next to me.
376:How was it? Coming to the airport with me was more fun than going to a mahjong dojo, right?
377:Chiori Mikami glances at me.
378:Wipe that smug look from your face. It's only because my mother is the best.
379:She stands on her tiptoes and waves hard in the direction the plane was flying.
380:...Don't feel bad. She'll return as soon she can.
381:I don't feel bad at all.
382:Are you acting tough again?
383:Not at all.
384:There's nothing to be sad about. My parents are outstanding adults, and outstanding adults are always busy. I also want to become an outstanding adult like my parents.
385:When that happens, I'll go to many places in the world to help lots and lots of people who need help. When that happens, I'll be as busy as them.
386:Probably because she just got a filling and is still not used to it in her mouth, she licks her gums as she speaks, which makes her funny condition seem especially cute.
387:Hmph... when that happens, you'll need to make an appointment with me a long, long time in advance when you want to play with me, you know?
388:This little lady seems to be less and less concerned about her image around me. Maybe this is something that I should be happy about.
389:No problem, I'll definitely reserve your time a long, long time in advance. Chiori, have you thought about what kind of adult you want to be in the future? Do you want to be a doctor like your mother?
390:Um... If I become a doctor, I'll have to wear a white coat all day long like my mother. I don't like that.
391:Oh, then do you want to become a physics professor like your father?
392:Yikes! I'll lose all my hair! That's too much of a sacrifice for me!
393:Haha!
394:Hmm... Hmm... Hmm... What should I become...?
395:Seeing her thinking really hard about this question, I touch her head.
396:It's okay. There's no need to rush. You can take your time when growing up. I'm sure you'll find your own unique answer, but before you do, can you promise me something?
397:Haha, are you going to take this opportunity to make a weird and excessive request again? I'm warning you, my mother isn't here to protect you right now.
398:I don't know if it's excessive, but I'm definitely not joking.
399:Can you stay by my side more often before you grow up and start exploring a bigger world?
400:The summer evening breeze blows gently between us, rustling her long golden hair. Chiori Mikami looks at me and blinks before suddenly turning her head away. Her action, however, fails to hide the upturned corners of her mouth.
401:Hmph! How dare you make such a request without my permission!
402:But... But... Since my mother kind of likes you, I'll reluctantly and temporarily agree to promise you that for one day so that I won't make her sad.
403:One day?
404:Of course! How can I promise something like this for a long period of time? It obviously depends on your future performance. Hmph! If you don't do well, I can leave you at any time!
405:Haha, I understand. One day it is.
406:In that case, take me home now.
407:Yes, my lady.
408:After 15 minutes, we meet Mrs. Mikami at a restaurant in the recreation area of the airport.
410:That's one more future appointment to be honored. Every day I spend in One Han City is so busy. Anyway, no matter what, I think I'll need to see Chiori Mikami to stop worrying all the time.
411:Oh, o-of course...
412:Having long been accustomed to all this, I just shake my head as I look at the smile on Chiori Mikami's face and think to myself that it's good as long as she is happy.
413:Oh, it's almost time for the dental appointment. We can get ready to go now.
414:...Dental appointment?
415:We don't say anything else until we arrive at the dental clinic. After checking the appointment details, the receptionist tells us to sit outside the consulting room and wait for our turn.
416:Dental Clinic
417:(Text Message) She only needs a filling for one tooth. Everything else is normal, so you don't need to worry about anything.
418:On the way to the mahjong dojo, after thinking it over several times, I decide to tell Mrs. Mikami about how Chiori Mikami resolved the conflict in the dental clinic, as well as her decision to go to a mahjong dojo.
